Actually, the typical iOS behavior is: when a modal is presented while the keyboard is up, the system dismisses the keyboard, and after the modal is dismissed, the keyboard automatically reappears if the input was previously focused. That's the root cause mentioned. So even if we dismiss keyboard before opening modal, the input still has focus, so after modal dismiss, iOS might bring the keyboard back. But if we explicitly dismiss the keyboard before modal opens, and the modal opening doesn't trigger the keyboard dismiss (since it's already dismissed), the system might not restore it.

